WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.372
This is Heimdall, built on Switch.

2
00:00:02.372 --> 00:00:04.140
Nothing merges without proof.

3
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:07.163
Agents write most of our code now.

4
00:00:07.163 --> 00:00:09.055
So pull requests got huge.

5
00:00:09.055 --> 00:00:10.218
This one's ours.

6
00:00:10.218 --> 00:00:13.710
Seventy-seven thousand lines, six hundred files.

7
00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.896
Nobody's reading all that.

8
00:00:15.896 --> 00:00:18.870
So a reviewer types LGTM, and hits merge.

9
00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:19.922
And the tests?

10
00:00:19.922 --> 00:00:23.191
The agent writes those too, and it writes them to pass.

11
00:00:23.191 --> 00:00:25.450
A test that can't fail proves nothing.

12
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:26.954
Heimdall fixes both.

13
00:00:26.954 --> 00:00:29.906
Reviewers that know what your developers know.

14
00:00:29.906 --> 00:00:33.500
And red tests, written from the ticket, before the code.

15
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.170
Here's how it works.

16
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.699
A ticket moves in Jira, or a PR opens on GitHub.

17
00:00:38.699 --> 00:00:46.050
Heimdall picks it up, wakes the right OpenCode agent, and runs every test inside a locked container.

18
00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.855
Switch is the backbone.

19
00:00:47.855 --> 00:00:49.854
Every agent gets an identity.

20
00:00:49.854 --> 00:00:51.577
Every ticket gets a room.

21
00:00:51.577 --> 00:00:55.850
And your team stays in Slack, Discord, Telegram or Mattermost.

22
00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:56.931
Watch it run.

23
00:00:56.931 --> 00:01:02.299
A real ticket moves to In Progress, with its money rules and acceptance criteria.

24
00:01:02.299 --> 00:01:03.889
Nobody touches Heimdall.

25
00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:06.341
Under a second later, there's a room.

26
00:01:06.341 --> 00:01:08.660
Seconds later, an agent is working.

27
00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:13.113
It writes tests from the ticket, and Heimdall runs them in the sandbox.

28
00:01:13.113 --> 00:01:15.540
They must fail, and for the right reason.

29
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.828
A test that passes before the feature exists gets rejected.

30
00:01:19.828 --> 00:01:25.000
What survives is pinned by hash, and runs in your CI on every pull request.

31
00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:26.008
Now, review.

32
00:01:26.008 --> 00:01:32.183
Heimdall captures what each developer knows: their docs, their history, their coding sessions.

33
00:01:32.183 --> 00:01:33.300
Secrets go first.

34
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.351
They approve it.

35
00:01:34.351 --> 00:01:38.490
It's signed, encrypted, and handed to their own reviewer agent.

36
00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:43.640
Beneath them, a Graphiti knowledge graph holds the team's decisions and incidents.

37
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.581
A developer raises the PR.

38
00:01:45.581 --> 00:01:46.574
The tests pass.

39
00:01:46.574 --> 00:01:49.685
Three reviewers start, cut off from each other.

40
00:01:49.685 --> 00:01:53.061
This one found that refunds can exceed the payment.

41
00:01:53.061 --> 00:01:55.510
And it wrote a failing test as proof.

42
00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.340
It lands on the exact line, on the pull request, and in chat.

43
00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.988
Then ten rules decide, in plain Go.

44
00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.514
No model in that path.

45
00:02:03.514 --> 00:02:07.260
Only a person can approve, and only that exact commit.

46
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.810
Setup is one prompt.

47
00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:12.799
Paste it into your coding agent, or run heimdall admin init.

48
00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:18.650
It connects GitHub, Jira and your chat, and drafts your context pack for you to approve.

49
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.527
And it's all Go, on one small VM.

50
00:02:21.527 --> 00:02:23.671
A forty-two megabyte server.

51
00:02:23.671 --> 00:02:25.968
A ten megabyte sandbox runner.

52
00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:28.724
Rootless containers with no network.

53
00:02:28.724 --> 00:02:29.719
Seven agents.

54
00:02:29.719 --> 00:02:30.485
Two cores.

55
00:02:30.485 --> 00:02:31.710
No public ports.

56
00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.532
Humans bring judgment.

57
00:02:33.532 --> 00:02:34.847
Agents bring proof.

58
00:02:34.847 --> 00:02:35.470
Heimdall.
